I inspected the change set: `src/project.rs`, the `run_test`/`run_cli` paths in `src/lib.rs`, `src/testing/{mod,harness,reporter}.rs`, `src/manifest.rs`, and the new discovery tests. The core logic (depth bound, symlink refusals, sorted discovery, zero-test guard, scaffold cleanup) is sound; the remaining issues are minor.

FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] src/lib.rs:226-234 — The project form prints `Tests run/Passed/Failed` and then, when `failed > 0`, calls `PrettyReporter::report`, which prints a second summary (`Test Results: ...` at src/testing/reporter.rs:65-82) and calls `std::process::exit(1)` (reporter.rs:120). So a failing `rb test` emits the counts twice and `run_test`, a `pub` library function, terminates the caller instead of returning `Err`; the explicit-path form has only the reporter summary. — Fix: have the project branch print only the reporter output on failure (or return an error and let `run_cli` exit). — VERIFIED: traced lib.rs:226-234 into reporter.rs:62-121.

2. [MINOR] src/project.rs:74-78 — `has_manifest` returns `true` for *any* `symlink_metadata` error other than `NotFound`, so an `EACCES` on `redblue.manifest` makes discovery claim the current directory as the project root even though it holds no manifest entry. `rb test` then fails with `Cannot inspect '<path>'` (project.rs:233-234) instead of the documented "No Redblue project found here" outcome (project.rs:34-41), and the walk never considers a valid ancestor. — Fix: match `Ok(_) => true`, `Err(NotFound) => false`, and surface other errors explicitly rather than treating them as presence; no test pins the permission-error case. — This is the only unverified branch I found; it is not reachable in the green path.

